      "settings": {
        "eyebrow": "Virtual staging near you",
        "heading": "Virtual Staging San Diego, CA",
        "lede": "Virtual staging is a digital marketing technique in real estate where a designer places true-to-scale 3D furniture, rugs and decor into photos of empty or cleared rooms, so buyers can see how each space lives before they visit. Bella's designers stage San Diego homes — coastal condos, bungalows and ADUs — in 24 to 48 hours, from {price:virtual-staging} a photo.",
        "cta_label": "Stage my listing — from {price:virtual-staging}",
        "cta_link": "/products/virtual-staging",
        "alt_label": "Browse the lookbook",
        "alt_link": "/pages/lookbook",
        "city": "San Diego",
        "market_heading": "Why virtual staging matters in the San Diego market",
        "market_text": "<p>San Diego's steady stream of military and defense-industry relocations means a constant pool of buyers shopping on short timelines from far away — buyers who rank listings almost entirely by photos before a whirlwind house-hunting trip. Home staging gets a listing shortlisted; empty photos get skipped.</p><p>And like the rest of coastal California, the lifestyle is the pitch: staged patios, decks and indoor-outdoor rooms let a La Jolla condo or a North Park bungalow sell the weather along with the walls.</p><p>The ADU boom adds a second job for staging here. A converted garage or granny flat is often the reason a buyer stretches for the property, but photographed empty it reads as storage. Staged as a studio with a bed, a table and a place to sit, it reads as the rental income or in-law suite the listing is really selling.</p><p>That's why the photos matter so much here: 97% of buyers use the internet in their home search, according to the National Association of Realtors. Virtual staging gives real estate agents a market-ready set of listing photos without scheduling a stager, a crew or a truck — and gives relocating buyers a reason to put the home on their shortlist.</p>",
        "local_heading": "Virtual home staging San Diego, neighborhood by neighborhood",
        "local_text": "<p>Designers stage coastal-casual for La Jolla, Pacific Beach and Encinitas, modern for downtown and East Village condos, and warm bungalow looks for North Park, South Park and Normal Heights.</p><p>Military relocation timelines drive a lot of the urgency, so photos come back in 24 to 48 hours — fast enough to list inside the window a PCS-ing buyer is actually house-hunting in.</p><p>Files upload to SDMLS or CRMLS with disclosure guidance built to California's AB 723 standard, and you keep full usage rights for the MLS, your website and social posts. There's no in-person consultation to schedule: order, upload and our design team handles the rest. Volume discounts apply automatically — 5% at 3+ photos, 10% at 6+, 15% at 11+ and 20% at 21+.</p>",
        "hoods_label": "Where we stage most",
        "hoods": "La Jolla, Pacific Beach, North Park, South Park, Normal Heights, Encinitas, Carlsbad, Chula Vista, Downtown, Point Loma"
      }
    },
